WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.125 --> 00:00:02.542
How do you feel in a space when...

00:00:02.792 --> 00:00:04.167
you have to be vulnerable?

00:00:04.250 --> 00:00:06.750
'Cause I have issues with vulnerability
and I'm a woman.

00:00:07.208 --> 00:00:09.417
I can take that one.
Yeah, that one I got.

00:00:09.500 --> 00:00:12.167
I want you both to take it,
so you just start, J.J.

00:00:12.250 --> 00:00:14.292
Well, excuse me.
I'll start with that one.

00:00:15.333 --> 00:00:18.125
I've realized just being vulnerable
in a character

00:00:18.208 --> 00:00:20.792
is easy for me,
because I do it in life,

00:00:20.875 --> 00:00:22.292
I'm open and honest, I don't...

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:25.542
You could judge me, it's fine. You know?

00:00:26.417 --> 00:00:29.208
I'm okay with that,
because I know who I am. Right?

00:00:29.292 --> 00:00:32.083
So, the more honest you are with yourself

00:00:32.667 --> 00:00:36.583
about who you are and your flaws,
and what shortcomings, and what not...

00:00:38.583 --> 00:00:40.333
being vulnerable is easier.

00:00:40.958 --> 00:00:42.167
That's been my experience.

00:00:42.250 --> 00:00:45.125
That's amazing.
Because for me, vulnerability is...

00:00:45.500 --> 00:00:47.583
is... When I feel vulnerable, I feel weak.

00:00:47.667 --> 00:00:49.833
It's like, I cannot be vulnerable,
this is so uncomfortable,

00:00:49.917 --> 00:00:51.375
I gotta go out here,
I gotta go somewhere else.

00:00:51.833 --> 00:00:55.333
You know, for me, it's always like,
I have to be protected.

00:00:55.417 --> 00:00:58.958
I feel most comfortable when I'm strong,
when it's not like,

00:00:59.042 --> 00:01:00.583
"I can't tell somebody I need help."

00:01:00.667 --> 00:01:02.250
You know what I mean?
Like, me? Hell no.

00:01:02.333 --> 00:01:04.458
I do my own thing, I'm independent.

00:01:04.542 --> 00:01:07.208
You know?
And at times, if... I'm learning now

00:01:07.292 --> 00:01:09.917
that it's okay, at times, to be, like...

00:01:10.625 --> 00:01:11.792
"Yes, please."

00:01:11.875 --> 00:01:13.375
You know what that is?
That's your ego.

00:01:13.458 --> 00:01:14.292
You think it's ego?

00:01:14.375 --> 00:01:16.458
Yeah, yeah. It's your ego
trying to protect itself.

00:01:16.708 --> 00:01:19.750
Ego isn't a bad word. Ego...
It's like, we all have an ego.

00:01:19.833 --> 00:01:20.667
Yes.

00:01:20.750 --> 00:01:23.375
It's a matter of having a balanced ego

00:01:23.458 --> 00:01:26.417
or a solid ego.
I don't wanna say strong ego, but like--

00:01:26.500 --> 00:01:28.208
-A balance. Just... Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:01:28.292 --> 00:01:30.250
When you're able
to withdraw from both... Yes.

00:01:30.333 --> 00:01:32.708
I have to agree with you. I never thought
about that, that's interesting.

00:01:32.792 --> 00:01:34.292
So I challenge myself

00:01:34.458 --> 00:01:36.792
whenever I feel, let's say,

00:01:36.875 --> 00:01:39.625
when my machismo may kick in and...

00:01:39.917 --> 00:01:42.167
let's say, a woman telling me something
about myself,

00:01:42.250 --> 00:01:45.417
saying I'm sensitive or something,
I'm like, "I ain't sensitive. Whatever."

00:01:45.500 --> 00:01:47.625
And then I check, I go,
"No, no, no. Let's check in.

00:01:47.708 --> 00:01:49.292
Let's check in. Maybe she's right.

00:01:49.375 --> 00:01:50.833
Maybe you are coming from a place
of this and that."

00:01:50.917 --> 00:01:54.708
And I'll make sure that I'll address it,
'cause I wanna understand.

00:01:54.792 --> 00:01:55.833
Right? I seek understanding.

00:01:56.458 --> 00:01:59.750
And then, let's say she's right,
I'm like, "You know what? You were right.

00:01:59.833 --> 00:02:03.292
That's me... That was triggered
by some part of me that..."

00:02:03.583 --> 00:02:06.167
You know, I'll be vulnerable and open
about whatever that is.

